1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,396
Chapter 4. The Trojan horse.

2
00:00:03,696 --> 00:00:11,243
On the other side of the world, Nintendo had been selling a family console since 1983: the Famicom.

3
00:00:11,423 --> 00:00:19,347
It wanted to reach the United States. But there, after the crash, stores didn't even want to hear the words video game.

4
00:00:19,897 --> 00:00:24,350
So Nintendo didn't sell a video game. It sold a toy.

5
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:34,266
They changed its shape, changed its name, and packed a robot next to it. On October 18, 1985, they tested it in New York.

6
00:00:34,446 --> 00:00:38,069
Exactly twenty-seven years after Tennis for Two.

7
00:00:38,249 --> 00:00:45,041
Among its games was one starring a plumber. Super Mario Bros. sold over 40 million copies.

8
00:00:45,221 --> 00:00:53,146
And in 1989, Nintendo put video games in your pocket: the Game Boy. With Tetris in the box.
